    "content": "Here's a practical guide to transport options on Provo:\n\nTaxis: Available at the airport and major resorts. Fares are fixed by zone — ask the driver before departing. Taxis are not metered.\n\nCar rental: Recommended if you're staying more than a few days. Driving is on the LEFT. A valid licence from your home country is accepted.\n\nBicycles: Some areas are bike-friendly, but be cautious on the main highway.\n\nRide sharing: Use the Transportation Hub in OneTCI to book rides with verified local operators.\n\nTip: Airport taxis can be busy during peak arrival times. Pre-booking through the OneTCI Transport Hub is recommended.",
